From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:50:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 200/207] dsv41 server: the compute default offers its tool to
 thinking chats only

Under TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE_DEFAULT=1 a chat with thinking off now gets no
built-in tool unless it lists code_interpreter itself. Unthinking, the prose
the model writes before a call is the visible answer, and the answer after
the result runs straight on into it ("Let me compute.232792560" on a TP2
dashboard check). The request's enable_thinking (or the server's default)
joins max_tokens, stop, logprobs and structured output in deciding whether
the default offers the tool. Thinking-off chats already got no runner guide.
---
